classDiagram
    class Owner {
        +str name
        +int available_minutes
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet: Pet) None
        +get_all_tasks() list~Task~
    }

    class Pet {
        +str name
        +str species
        +int age
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task: Task) None
    }

    class Task {
        +str description
        +int duration_minutes
        +str priority
        +str time
        +str frequency
        +bool completed
        +str pet_name
        +date due_date
        +int start_minutes
        +int end_minutes
        +mark_complete() None
        +next_occurrence(today: date) Task
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +list~Task~ plan
        +list~Task~ skipped
        +int minutes_used
        +filter_tasks(pet_name: str, completed: bool) list~Task~
        +generate_plan(today: date) list~Task~
        +sort_by_priority(tasks: list~Task~) list~Task~
        +sort_by_time(tasks: list~Task~) list~Task~
        +mark_task_complete(task: Task, today: date) Task
        +detect_conflicts(tasks: list~Task~) list~str~
        +explain_plan() str
        -_conflict_message(first: Task, second: Task)$ str
    }

    Owner "1" *-- "*" Pet : owns
    Pet "1" *-- "*" Task : has
    Scheduler "1" --> "1" Owner : plans for
    Scheduler "1" o-- "*" Task : plan / skipped
    Task ..> Task : next_occurrence() creates
    Scheduler ..> Pet : mark_task_complete() adds next task to

    note for Task "time is normalized to HH:MM on creation.<br>start_minutes and end_minutes are read-only properties<br>(None when the task has no time).<br>next_occurrence() returns None for 'once' tasks."
    note for Scheduler "minutes_used is a read-only property.<br>PRIORITY_ORDER: high=3, medium=2, low=1<br>RECURRENCE_DAYS: daily=1, weekly=7"
